# Production targets — modern evergreen browsers only.
#
# AHO ships to Cloudflare Pages with Next.js. The default Next.js
# browserslist resolves to includes IE 11-era polyfills which Lighthouse
# (2026-05-16 audit) flagged as Legacy JavaScript wasting ~11 KiB on the
# first-party chunk + bloating eval time.
#
# Targets here cover Chrome 109+ (2023-01), Firefox 102+ (2022-06),
# Safari 16+ (2022-09), Edge 109+ (2023-01) — covers >97% of the
# real-estate traffic we expect (agent + buyer market segments are
# typically on current mobile + recent desktop).
#
# Bump these when Lighthouse audits show further savings AND telemetry
# (when PostHog is wired) confirms no real users on older targets.
#
# `[production]` scopes these to `next build`; dev keeps the broader
# default so HMR / SWC don't get surprised by polyfill differences.

[production]
last 2 Chrome versions
last 2 Firefox versions
last 2 Safari versions
last 2 Edge versions
last 2 ChromeAndroid versions
last 2 FirefoxAndroid versions
last 2 iOS versions
not dead

[development]
last 1 Chrome version
last 1 Firefox version
last 1 Safari version
